        },
        "texto": "Saharonim, here translated ornaments, is in Isaiah 3:18 rendered “round tires like the moon.” In Judges 8:26 it is said that there were chains about the camels’ necks. It thus appears that these camels had gold chains around their necks on which were the saharonim, or little moon…"
      },
      "c-a7cbe78b06c5c8f4": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-232",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Baal-berith, or the covenant Baal, was one of the numerous Baalim that the Israelites worshiped at different times. We have no definite description of this god. A temple was built for him at Shechem (Judges 9:46), but what were the special ceremonies we do not know. The worship i…"
      }
    },
